Subject: [PATCH v3 7/6] libexec/mail: Leave published work in place
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: orqpullwrqqrwqystttnrzykuzryrzqz

Once Pat publishes my patches in b/dev, they become immutable, but
they are still mine and still off trunk. get-up-to-date.sh then tries
to rebase them onto trunk, jj refuses, and just process-email stops
before it reads any mail.

Work built on b/dev, including the working copy, would also be moved
onto trunk and lose the merge it was built against. The process-email
skill repeats the revset to judge what is left open, so it changes in
step.
---
change-id: orqpullwrqqrwqystttnrzykuzryrzqz

This fixes a failure the series hits once b/dev carries it. It sits on
top of 6/6 and can be taken or left on its own.

 .claude/skills/process-email/SKILL.md | 3 ++-
 libexec/mail/get-up-to-date.sh        | 7 +++++--
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.claude/skills/process-email/SKILL.md b/.claude/skills/process-email/SKILL.md
index 172bc32..5125d3d 100644
--- a/.claude/skills/process-email/SKILL.md
+++ b/.claude/skills/process-email/SKILL.md
@@ -50,7 +50,8 @@ Before any work, bring in everything that has landed since the last
 pass, on both trunk and the list. One recipe does the mechanical part:
 
     me="$(whoami)"
-    work='mine() ~ ::trunk@upstream ~ (::mail@upstream ~ root())::'
+    work='mine() ~ ::trunk@upstream ~ (::mail@upstream ~ root())::
+        ~ (immutable() ~ ::trunk@upstream)::'
     cd ~/lab/default.jj
     just get-up-to-date
 
diff --git a/libexec/mail/get-up-to-date.sh b/libexec/mail/get-up-to-date.sh
index 462c01d..3e295b2 100755
--- a/libexec/mail/get-up-to-date.sh
+++ b/libexec/mail/get-up-to-date.sh
@@ -28,8 +28,11 @@ readonly PROGNAME="${0##*/}"
 
 # Your commits off trunk, less everything descended from the list.
 # Trunk and the list share no commit but root(), so the outbox is left
-# out however far the list has moved since it was built on.
-readonly WORK='mine() ~ ::trunk@upstream ~ (::mail@upstream ~ root())::'
+# out however far the list has moved since it was built on. Anything
+# built on a published head other than trunk, such as b/dev, is left
+# where it is; that covers your own patches once Pat publishes them.
+readonly WORK='mine() ~ ::trunk@upstream ~ (::mail@upstream ~ root())::
+    ~ (immutable() ~ ::trunk@upstream)::'
 
 err() {
 	echo "E: ${PROGNAME}: ${*}" >&2

